<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sibylla Augusta of Saxe-Lauenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1675–1733</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Margravine Sibylla Augusta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sibylla Augusta of Saxe-Lauenburg was the wife of Margrave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-william-margrave-of-baden-baden">Louis William of Baden-Baden</a>, the commander known as 'Turkish Louis'. After his death in 1707 she ruled the margraviate as regent for her sons until 1727. She completed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> residence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rastatt">Rastatt</a> and built the Favorite palace nearby, with its collection of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porcelain">porcelain</a> and faience.</p></div>
